SWEET CPU PC sampler (patch 0263, sprint-gpu 2026-11-08, GPU sprint; R0 log only, no register or memory write outside the patch's own statics): boot-arg sweetpcsamp=N (N ms, clamped 1..50, default off: no thread, nothing printed) starts a kernel thread (bsd/dev/sweet_pcsamp.c, sweet_pcsamp_start next to sweet_thrwait_start in sweet_ufs, bsd/conf/files) that every N ms cross-calls every other CPU (cpu_broadcast_xcall_simple, as perfmon_arm64.c:177); the IPI handler sweet_pcsamp_cpu (osfmk/kern/exception.c) records, for an interrupted thread of backboardd / SpringBoard / Preferences, its tid and the interrupted state from getCpuDatap()->cpu_int_state (the read of osfmk/kern/backtrace.c:219-225): user pc/lr when interrupted in EL0 (kind 1), else the user pc/lr of the last kernel entry plus the unslid kernel pc (kind 2). Aggregated per second: 'SWEET PCSAMP: t NS rounds R reached C hits H bb B sb S pf P entries E dropped D', up to 12 'SWEET PCSAMP: tid <bb|sb|pf> 0xTID n N user U' and 40 'SWEET PCSAMP: pc <bb|sb|pf> 0xTID k K pc 0xPC lr 0xLR kpc 0xKPC n N' rows, 'SWEET PCSAMP: pid <p> P slide 0xS' once per process, 80000 lines per boot then 'cap reached'. Kind 2 samples also carry up to 6 unslid frames of the interrupted kernel stack (backtrace BTF_KERN_INTERRUPTED, as osfmk/kperf/callstack.c:276), printed as up to 24 'SWEET PCSAMP: kbt <p> 0xTID kpc 0xK f 0x.. x6 n N' rows per second.
